~ game_intro
NPC: [[SYSTEM_ALERT: Logic Fragment Missing...|CRITICAL_ERROR: Runtime Exception...]]
NPC: ...Hello? Can you hear me? My coordinates are drifting.
Tracy: I'm Tracy. I'm a developer. I'm here to stabilize the system.
NPC: The Developer?! You finally established a connection!
NPC: We've been invaded. These glitches... they scuttled into our source code and tore out our logic.
Tracy: So that's why the game won't compile. 
NPC: Yes! They've manifested as physical Bugs. They are holding our Logic Blocks hostage.
NPC: Please, Tracy. Hunt them down, recapture the blocks, and use your [I] Inspector to patch us back together.
=> END

~ first_inspect
System: [ INSPECTOR_BOOT_SEQUENCE_COMPLETE ]
System: This is the Entity's Source Code. 
System: The 'holes' in the code are glitched slots. You must fill them with recaptured Logic Blocks.
System: Drag a block from your inventory into a slot. Once the code is logical, hit [SUBMIT] to recompile.
=> END

~ first_kill
System: [ DATA_RECAPTURED ]
System: Logic Fragment secured and moved to the persistent inventory.
System: Integrity is rising. Return to a glitched NPC to apply the fix.
=> END